uped","confidence":0.776,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-78-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7069009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8884c9fdc77576f42bcdd9046d7626561e51e9f9bbd3421d7abc4b0e766a7954","compact":"14adf3b8ed1c46ec882c6b4e90c5a7fecd4a533ae24c01579dbdddb94d666c06","nasal":"14adf3b8ed1c46ec882c6b4e90c5a7fecd4a533ae24c01579dbdddb94d666c06"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-69-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":69,"verse":10,"english":"Having performed hard penances in this forest, for three thousand years I at last attained to the region of Brahmā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.868,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-78-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7069010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ebe537d7fea7d9a9eddaef9990cf437f5afb7cb09b1b6be3594e9057719933af","compact":"4adcdb090cb85d20c2ba49ce43abcf3a223d638d220289ed1062a6fa352274d4","nasal":"4adcdb090cb85d20c2ba49ce43abcf3a223d638d220289ed1062a6fa352274d4"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-69-11","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":69,"verse":11,"english":"And albeit I had reached the Brahmā region I was still being assailed by hunger and thirst. And gradually I grew tired therewith.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.559,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-78-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7069011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e714395af96247d38ce8024203ca737798a6b2c44f7e05c86a8646a4ff0c5f51","compact":"f2ed0b03a99ca6562ee180a8e7551d0780e1025cd41c606041796b81fdb37775","nasal":"08d13f7001f71b36bf4bc8ca22b27a3d1f5003d8ecd55eb25eddc573eeab1100"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-69-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":69,"verse":12,"english":"There upon approaching the patriarch Brahma, the lord of three worlds, I said: O lord, here there is no hunger or thirst; still why have I been brought to their control? Of what iniquity of mine is this fruit? O deity, tell me upon what I shall live.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.953,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-78-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7069012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b97363b94119fb40788922642bb7ef2f2d548dfa0c51756d82d7599f982d29fc","compact":"4edcbecc9f7dde021cd93e6065b5433b988f016ff3776a81ebd82a7f37391698","nasal":"4edcbecc9f7dde021cd93e6065b5433b988f016ff3776a81ebd82a7f37391698"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-69-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":69,"verse":13,"english":"There upon approaching the patriarch Brahma, the lord of three worlds, I said: O lord, here there is no hunger or thirst; still why have I been brought to their control? Of what iniquity of mine is this fruit? O deity, tell me upon what I shall live.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.574,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-78-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7069013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2a12d46a1be64a1fe6ba0bbda2706d650d402af30e4c2a80b14ab9c98b224d1c","compact":"559d48766056b73b67a4e4374125b1fcf70c0a1e82776e932fe78ad7f9767b5c","nasal":"559d48766056b73b67a4e4374125b1fcf70c0a1e82776e932fe78ad7f9767b5c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-69-14","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":69,"verse":14,"english":"Whereto the patriarch replied: O son of Sudeva, do you live upon sweet savoured meat everyday.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-78-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7069014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"59d23ba4edb34e82f863f245886cc118dc3d44ff9692e196b7d2