-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":69,"verse":17,"english":"Thereupon do you now live upon your own dead body fostered by various food. By this you shall keep up your being.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.651,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-78-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7069017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d2c065f921c0dc306a92fceaecadcda2d943bfcd937757847ab3206b6975b79e","compact":"3a6b2d18db92bda1313e9cc1354d21d56da0b24c1daa750b6a4063d851cbb252","nasal":"d2513d5a989f9ff1daf40bb518bd17322148f25bfd6ec28f945b86e44e2abcbc"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-69-18","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":69,"verse":18,"english":"O Sveta, you shall be relived from this affliction when the irrepressible, great Saint Agastya shall reach that forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.614,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-78-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7069018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5574c045d6ad8322d6eb908a83d8cfe59a810fea8a1d6d27ca893c098113d35f","compact":"f39f04ff7545974f5090acf1e3af6d2c8ae7e0187d895668556414313993db00","nasal":"f39f04ff7545974f5090acf1e3af6d2c8ae7e0187d895668556414313993db00"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-69-19","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":69,"verse":19,"english":"O gentle one, even to the immortals he can give salvation; what wonder it is that he shall relieve you from the miseries of hunger and thirst.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-78-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7069019","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1f21ec98c755cac98339431ad80739b9f5a2a30febfcf43211f7785f3171f21a","compact":"9282746c1ec89faa7983580c07f42cf1653b57cc567fcb4ff5865463629f429a","nasa