ious Agastya born of a Kumbha; for none else is capable of coming here; do you therefore save me from this pain, who am afflicted with great miseries.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.662,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-78-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7069022","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"12f9972f4dac08fddcb0d03ec8fe5831380cbb4b19e56bbb269ce43a0bf39baf","compact":"9e613cc89fdfe0f48bc26356efa6ceb39a1981a3bb0fca2509e6c1389a27eed7","nasal":"d31ea41b7c67622b4be0293176f227df80ea139a0ee5fcbf57d4af7e305da84f"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-69-23","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":69,"verse":23,"english":"O foremost of twice-born ones, O gentle one, do you take this ornament; may good betide you. Do you be propitiated with me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.612,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-78-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7069023","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3b405ee13d89b800351f3df927488f25a52180b7332806fedc0cb9bb47b0726c","compact":"37e57decef4025ed9472bd35a256f7d444ea096a8712ecee5ce05a9a5b244c30","nasal":"37e57decef4025ed9472bd35a256f7d444ea096a8712ecee5ce05a9a5b244c30"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-69-24","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":69,"verse":24,"english":"Hearing those words of the heavenly being, exciting pity, I accepted this ornament for saving him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-78-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7069024","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a58303ad9bfac4b48e1b403a0039141d159e1470f80a620427629508b3c351f4","compact":"46915e799bc77a86dc7ec5de79e5791ef233631bdda5109bfecccde544f9902c","nasal":"46915e799bc77a86dc7ec5de79e5791ef233631bdda5109bfecccde544f9